# Call-site ledger of more-itertools at 4aeb4338ae1407d8da9723e86da99efeb446f719.
# See macro-benchmark/README.md; more-itertools.md gives the judgements.
#
# Supported: CPython and PyPy 3.11 and later (pyproject.toml requires-python
# >=3.11; classifiers; CI matrix 3.11 to 3.15 and pypy-3.11). Version
# branches that run: math.sumprod is missing on 3.11, so more.py:188-212
# defines dl_split, dl_mul and _fsumprod, and recipes.py:298 binds _sumprod
# to dotproduct; recipes.batched is the wrapper of itertools.batched from
# 3.13 (recipes.py:952) and _batched before it; the max-heap functions of
# heapq exist from 3.14 (recipes.py:105), so running_median uses
# _running_median_minheap_and_maxheap there and _running_median_minheap_only
# before.
#
# The iterable role (README, "Rulings for batch 6": declared iterable
# types; more-itertools.md, "The iterable role" and "Contracts"). Every
# parameter that the shipped stubs (*.pyi, which count as annotations) type
# as an iterable or iterator of unconstrained items (Iterable[_T],
# Iterator[_T], Iterable[Any], _T | Iterable[_T]) is one ordinary
# source-iterable role. Its package members: numeric_range and SequenceView
# (Sequence at runtime); peekable, seekable, islice_extended, sized_iterator,
# time_limited, callback_iter, countable and serialize (Iterator[_T] bases in
# more.pyi); and the _concurrent_tee objects that concurrent_tee returns.
# Not a member: bucket (a Container in the stub). Package generators may
# reach the role, but advancing a generator is no call. The items of a
# client iterable are client values (B3).
# Narrower contracts keep a separate purpose requirement (the same
# ruling): a Sequence parameter admits numeric_range and SequenceView (a
# matrix, SequenceView only); an iterable of numbers or indices
# (Iterable[int], Iterable[float], Iterable[_NumberT]) admits compatible
# numeric_range objects only, the documented producer of numeric ranges; the
# outer iterable of an iterable of iterables, tuples or mappings admits no
# member, except at transpose, where matmul forwards its SequenceView matrix
# (recipes.py:1051); inner Iterable[_T] values are source iterables.
# What a member runs:
#   iter(v): the __iter__ of the nine iterator classes (each returns self)
#     and numeric_range.__iter__ (a takewhile over a generator expression);
#     a SequenceView gets the library Sequence.__iter__, a generator;
#   advancing iter(v): the nine __next__, and SequenceView.__getitem__
#     (called by Sequence.__iter__); the numeric_range iterator calls no
#     package code;
#   len(v) and the length hint of list(), tuple(), sorted(), str.join,
#     f(*v), [*v] and itertools.product: numeric_range.__len__,
#     SequenceView.__len__, sized_iterator.__len__;
#   truth test: numeric_range.__bool__, peekable.__bool__, seekable.__bool__,
#     and __len__ of SequenceView and sized_iterator (no __bool__).
# A lazy library object (islice, zip, map, chain, ...) that the function
# returns is advanced by the client: only what its construction calls is an
# edge of the function (islice, zip, map, filter, enumerate, compress,
# takewhile, dropwhile, starmap, groupby, tee, cycle, zip_longest,
# accumulate and chain.from_iterable call iter() on their iterable argument
# at once; chain calls iter() on its arguments only when advanced).
default reject more_itertools.more.SequenceView.__getitem__, more_itertools.more.bucket.__getitem__, more_itertools.more.islice_extended.__getitem__, more_itertools.more.numeric_range.__getitem__, more_itertools.more.peekable.__getitem__, more_itertools.more.seekable.__getitem__: the operand of this site is no package object of these classes: it is a builtin or library object (list, tuple, deque, dict, str, range, typing construct, ...), a package generator, or a client value outside the iterable and sequence roles (header); the sites that subscript a role value, or iterate a SequenceView (Sequence.__iter__ calls its __getitem__), accept these explicitly
default reject more_itertools.more._concurrent_tee.__next__, more_itertools.more.callback_iter.__next__, more_itertools.more.countable.__next__, more_itertools.more.islice_extended.__next__, more_itertools.more.peekable.__next__, more_itertools.more.seekable.__next__, more_itertools.more.serialize.__next__, more_itertools.more.sized_iterator.__next__, more_itertools.more.time_limited.__next__: this site advances no package iterator: the iterated object is a builtin or library object, a package generator, or a client value outside the iterable role (header), or the advancing happens later in client code; the sites that advance a role value in this function accept these explicitly
